G4 one constant across hosts (rms of log a0_equiv <= 0.1 dex):
 MBII subsamples (luminosity / central split, not host-mass bins): full 2.01, bright 3.05, faint 1.151, centrals Mh>1e12/h 3.491; rms over bright/faint/centrals 0.217 dex, range 0.486 dex [FAIL, PARTIAL proxy]
 ZOMG centrals 1.40 vs satellites 1.48: diff 0.024 dex (environment split, not host mass; PARTIAL proxy, within 0.1)
 EAGLE (feedback variants move galaxies ALONG the relation), NIHAO (scatter by M*, no g_dag per bin), MUGS2, Magneticum, FIRE-2: NOT TESTABLE.
 Reported intrinsic RAR scatter (not G4): MUGS2 0.06, EAGLE 0.08, NIHAO 0.079 (0.04 at M* 1e9.3-1e11, 0.11 below), ZOMG centrals 0.048, satellites 0.192, MBII ~0.1 full.

G5 operative: halo + baryon gravity in every simulation: PASS by definition. Grudic20 scale built from G, m_p, sigma_T: carries no rho_DE, so G2 slope 0 if it were the mechanism.

Rival language. Passing shows freedom, not evidence. kappa = 1/2 FITTED; not theory closed.
